Subject: [PATCH] mailbox: qcom-ipcc: mask summary IRQ in SM-X910 suspend

The Samsung SM-X910 firmware returns from PSCI SYSTEM_SUSPEND whenever the
ADSP raises its SMP2P signal through the APSS IPCC frame.  Linux records no
wake IRQ because the IPCC summary handler is requested with IRQF_NO_SUSPEND;
ftrace shows IRQ 13 (ipcc_0) followed by IRQ 16 (smp2p-adsp) on the spurious
resume path.

Keep upstream behavior on other platforms.  On gts9uwifi, let the IRQ core
mask the IPCC summary interrupt during system suspend.  Pending DSP messages
remain in the IPCC receive registers and are dispatched after a legitimate
resume.

--- a/drivers/mailbox/qcom-ipcc.c
+++ b/drivers/mailbox/qcom-ipcc.c
@@ -283,6 +283,7 @@ static int qcom_ipcc_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	u32 config_value;
 	static int id;
 	char *name;
+	unsigned long irqflags = IRQF_TRIGGER_HIGH | IRQF_NO_THREAD;
 	int ret;
 
 	ipcc = devm_kzalloc(&pdev->dev, sizeof(*ipcc), GFP_KERNEL);
@@ -320,9 +321,12 @@ static int qcom_ipcc_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	if (ret)
 		goto err_mbox;
 
+	/* Mask IPCC DSP traffic during SM-X910 system suspend. */
+	if (!of_machine_is_compatible("samsung,gts9uwifi"))
+		irqflags |= IRQF_NO_SUSPEND;
+
 	ret = devm_request_irq(&pdev->dev, ipcc->irq, qcom_ipcc_irq_fn,
-			       IRQF_TRIGGER_HIGH | IRQF_NO_SUSPEND |
-			       IRQF_NO_THREAD, name, ipcc);
+			       irqflags, name, ipcc);
 	if (ret < 0) {
 		dev_err(&pdev->dev, "Failed to register the irq: %d\n", ret);
 		goto err_req_irq;
